    "question": "What is overfitting and how can it be detected?",
    "k": 5,
    "source_filter": null,
    "model": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite",
    "answer": "Overfitting occurs when a model is fit too closely to the particularities of the training set, allowing it to perform well on the training data but failing to generalize to new data [2]. \n\nIt can be detected by comparing the model's performance on the training set versus the test set, specifically when there is a large discrepancy where the training set score is much higher than the test set score [3].",
